 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The web process uses the shared `sessions` instance in [the session store](../../larder/session_store.py)
+([keep sessions in memory](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-memory.md)).
+
+## Known limits
+
+- A restart or deploy clears sessions. Members must log in again afterward; deploy outside opening hours to reduce
+  disruption.
+- Separate web processes do not share sessions. Use one web process, or sticky routing to keep a member's requests
+  on the same process; sticky routing still loses sessions on restart.
+- Stored entries are not automatically removed on expiry. Callers must enforce the session lifetime; restarting
+  the process clears accumulated entries and logs everyone out.
 
